// prompt: the row tags of the one K-AT input relation factAtom(tag, u, a, x, y) (a closed set; the rule text of Gate.f5fRules matches
// the numbers of Gate.factTagNumber). For atom node a: FactHead (x = the unit its head names by exact name), FactAssert (x = the
// assertion node p), FactArity (x = term count), FactLeftLocal / FactRightLocal (x = the local binder of term 0 / 1), FactLeftLiteral /
// FactRightLiteral (x = the int literal of term 0 / 1), FactHeadName (x = the symbol of the head text, joined with the kernel prelude
// relations Srs.Facts.*). FactCredit is per assertion node a = p: x = the statement s of block y that p dominates the rest of (a bare
// `@<..>` statement or the value of a val statement); only these credit their proved atoms. The walker writes syntax only.
enum Gate.FactTag:
  case Gate.FactHead
  case Gate.FactAssert
  case Gate.FactArity
  case Gate.FactLeftLocal
  case Gate.FactLeftLiteral
  case Gate.FactRightLocal
  case Gate.FactRightLiteral
  case Gate.FactHeadName
  case Gate.FactCredit

